src/screens/OrdersScreen.tsx.fix:
Never early-return before all hooks. Do the redirect in an effect and gate the JSX after every hook has run:

  useEffect(() => { if (needsAuth()) navigation.navigate('LoginGate', { reason: 'orders' }); }, [needsAuth, navigation]);
  // ...ALL other hooks unchanged...
  if (needsAuth()) {
    return (<SafeAreaView ...>{/* skeleton */}</SafeAreaView>);
  }
  if (loading) { ... }
  return ( ...main... );

Move the needsAuth() JSX guard down next to the `if (loading)` block so hook order is identical on every render.

Decouple fetch from filter. Make loadOrders independent of filters:

  const loadOrders = useCallback(async (refresh=false) => { ...; const userOrders = await OrderService.getUserOrders(refresh); setOrders(userOrders); }, [isAuthenticated]);

Re-filter reactively instead of inside loadOrders:

  useEffect(() => { filterOrders(orders, selectedStatus, selectedDateFilter, searchQuery); }, [orders, selectedStatus, selectedDateFilter, searchQuery, filterOrders]);

Now loadOrders is stable and the focus effect no longer re-fires on keystrokes/filter taps. Remove the direct filterOrders() calls from loadOrders and the handlers.

Only show the full skeleton on the first cold load; refresh silently afterward:

  if (refresh) { setRefreshing(true); }
  else if (orders.length === 0) { setLoading(true); }

So returning to an already-loaded screen re-fetches in the background without wiping the list.

